/-!
# Von Neumann's inequality and A-stable time stepping

**Von Neumann's inequality** ([VonNeumann1951]): for a contraction `T` (`‖T‖ ≤ 1`) of a complex
inner product space and a complex polynomial `p`, `‖p(T)‖ ≤ sup_{|ζ| = 1} |p(ζ)|`
(`VonNeumann.inequality`); no completeness is needed. On a Hilbert space it extends to rational
functions `p/q` without poles in the closed unit disc: `q(T)` is invertible and
`‖p(T) q(T)⁻¹‖ ≤ sup_{|ζ| = 1} |p(ζ)/q(ζ)|` (`VonNeumann.inequality_rational`).

**Von Neumann's theorem in the half-plane and A-stable one-step schemes** ([HairerWanner1996],
§IV.3 and §IV.11): a rational function `r = p/q` without poles in the closed left half-plane
defines the one-step scheme `u ↦ r(τA) u` for `u' = A u`; it is A-stable if `|r(iy)| ≤ 1` on the
imaginary axis (by the maximum principle, `|r| ≤ 1` on the closed left half-plane). For every
dissipative operator `A` (`re ⟪A x, x⟫ ≤ 0`), every step `τ` and every `n`,
`‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ (sup_y |r(iy)|)ⁿ`: for bounded `A` and `τ ≥ 0` with `r(τA) = p(τA) q(τA)⁻¹`
(`VonNeumann.inequality_dissipative`), and for m-dissipative, possibly unbounded, `A` (the
generators of contraction semigroups, [Pazy1983], §1.4) and `τ > 0` with `r(τA)` through the
resolvent `S = (1 - τA)⁻¹`, for `deg p ≤ deg q` (`r` bounded at infinity, as `r(τA)` must be
for unbounded `A`): `r(τA) = P(S) Q(S)⁻¹` for `P(s) = sᴺ p(1 - 1/s)` and `Q(s) = sᴺ q(1 - 1/s)`,
`N = deg q`, polynomials since `1 - 1/s = τA` at `s = S`; for bounded `A` this is
`p(τA) Sᴺ (q(τA) Sᴺ)⁻¹ = p(τA) q(τA)⁻¹` (`VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative`). These are
stated for complex `r` on complex Hilbert spaces, and for real `r` (the stability functions of
Runge–Kutta methods) on real or complex Hilbert spaces (`VonNeumann.inequality_dissipative_real`,
`VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative_real`). The suprema are taken in `[0, ∞]`. So an A-stable
scheme is unconditionally stable, `‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ 1` for every step and every `n`. The proof is von
Neumann's inequality for the Cayley transform `C_τ = (1 + τA)(1 - τA)⁻¹`, the unique bounded
operator mapping `x - τAx` to `x + τAx`, a contraction (`VonNeumann.cayley_contraction`), and
`r̃(w) = r((w - 1)/(w + 1))`.

**The error of an A-stable scheme of order `m`** ([BrennerThomee1979]): if moreover
`r(z) - e^z = O(z^{m+1})` at `0`, there is a constant `K`, depending on `r` only, such that
`‖r(τA)ⁿ x - e^{nτA} x‖ ≤ K nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖` for every bounded dissipative `A`, `τ ≥ 0`, `n`
and `x`: for complex `r` on every complex Hilbert space (`VonNeumann.error_bound`), for real `r`
on every real or complex Hilbert space (`VonNeumann.error_bound_real`). The same bound, with the
same constant, holds for every m-dissipative, possibly unbounded, `A`, `τ > 0` and
`x ∈ D(A^{m+1})`, with `r(τA)` through the resolvent and `e^{tA}` the contraction semigroup
generated by `A` ([BrennerThomee1979]): `VonNeumann.error_bound_mdissipative`
(complex `r`), `VonNeumann.error_bound_mdissipative_real` (real `r`). Mathlib has no
`C₀`-semigroups: the semigroup is the family `S` of bounded operators with `S 0 = 1` whose orbits
`t ↦ S t x`, `x ∈ D(A)`, are the strong solutions of `u' = A u` (`VonNeumann.IsStrongSolution`),
unique, so `S t` is determined on `D(A)`; `x ∈ D(A^{m+1})` with `A^{m+1} x = y` is a chain
`u 0 = x, …, u (m + 1) = y` with `(u j, u (j + 1))` in the graph of `A`.

**Quasi-contractive semigroups and Banach spaces** ([BrennerThomee1979]). For `A` with `A - ω`
m-dissipative (`‖e^{tA}‖ ≤ e^{ωt}`) and an A-stable scheme of order `m` the bound holds with
exponential growth, `K e^{κωnτ} nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖`, for `ωτ ≤ c₀`, `c₀`, `K`, `κ` depending on `r`
only (`VonNeumann.error_bound_quasi_real`). On a Banach space, for a strongly continuous
semigroup with generator `A`, stability of `r(τA)` and boundedness of the remainder are not
automatic; given them, the bound holds with the stability constant
(`VonNeumann.error_bound_banach_real`). For bounded semigroups of real or complex Banach spaces
and A-stable `r` with `|r(∞)| < 1` both are theorems: the Hille–Phillips functional calculus
(on the complexification, for real spaces) gives
`Q(R)` invertible, `‖ρ(τA)‖` bounded and Brenner–Thomée's stability bound
`‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ M (1 + C √n)` ([BrennerThomee1979]), so the order-`m` error holds with the `√n`
loss of the stability bound, i.e. with rate `τ^{m-1/2}` at fixed `T = nτ`
(`VonNeumann.error_bound_banach_sqrt`). The sources' smooth-data rate `τᵐ`, without `√n`
([HershKato1979], for `x ∈ D(A^{m+2})`), is not formalized.

The operator `p(T)` is `Polynomial.aeval T p`; `q(T)⁻¹` is `Ring.inverse` in the Banach algebra
of bounded operators; a real polynomial acts over `𝕜` through `Polynomial.map (algebraMap ℝ 𝕜)`;
`e^{tA}` is `NormedSpace.exp`.

**Hille–Yosida on Banach spaces** ([Pazy1983], §1.5). A strongly continuous semigroup with
`‖S(t)‖ ≤ M e^{ωt}` has the half-plane `re z > ω` in the resolvent set of its generator, with
`‖(z - A)⁻ᵐ‖ ≤ M/(re z - ω)ᵐ` (`VonNeumann.resolvent_estimates_banach`). For `ωτ ≤ c` they make
`Q(R)` invertible and bound the remainder `ρ(τA)`, so the bound of
`VonNeumann.error_bound_banach_real` holds with only the stability of `r(τA)` assumed
(`VonNeumann.error_bound_banach_real_hille_yosida`); for backward Euler, `r(τA) = R`, the
stability is the Hille–Yosida estimate and the bound needs nothing beyond the growth bound
(`VonNeumann.error_bound_backward_euler_banach`).

## References

* [J. von Neumann, *Eine Spektraltheorie für allgemeine Operatoren eines unitären Raumes*][VonNeumann1951]
* [E. Hairer, G. Wanner, *Solving Ordinary Differential Equations II*][HairerWanner1996], §IV.3
  (A-stability, order), §IV.11 (contractivity, von Neumann's theorem)
* [A. Pazy, *Semigroups of Linear Operators and Applications to Partial Differential Equations*][Pazy1983], §1.4, §1.5, §3.1
* [P. Brenner, V. Thomée, *On Rational Approximations of Semigroups*][BrennerThomee1979]
* [R. Hersh, T. Kato, *High-Accuracy Stable Difference Schemes for Well-Posed Initial-Value Problems*][HershKato1979]
* [V. Thomée, *Galerkin Finite Element Methods for Parabolic Problems*][Thomee2006], Ch. 7, 9

Bibliography: [references.bib](../../docs/references.bib)
-/

open scoped InnerProductSpace Topology
open Polynomial Asymptotics

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace VonNeumann

/-- `u` is a **strong solution** of `u' = A u` on `I`: continuous on `I`, and at every `t ∈ I`,
`u t` lies in the domain of `A` and `u` has the derivative `A (u t)` within `I`. -/
def IsStrongSolution {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace 𝕜 E]
    [NormedSpace ℝ E] (A : E →ₗ.[𝕜] E) (I : Set ℝ) (u : ℝ → E) : Prop :=
  ContinuousOn u I ∧ ∀ t ∈ I, ∃ v, (u t, v) ∈ A.graph ∧ HasDerivWithinAt u v I t

/-- **Von Neumann's inequality** ([VonNeumann1951]). For a contraction `T` of a complex inner
product space `E`, not necessarily complete, and a complex polynomial `p`,
`‖p(T)‖ ≤ sup_{|ζ| = 1} |p(ζ)|`. -/
theorem inequality {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E] {T : E →L[ℂ] E}
    (hT : ‖T‖ ≤ 1) (p : ℂ[X]) :
    ‖aeval T p‖ₑ ≤ ⨆ ζ ∈ Metric.sphere (0 : ℂ) 1, ‖p.eval ζ‖ₑ := by
  sorry

/-- **Von Neumann's inequality for rational functions** ([VonNeumann1951]). For a contraction
`T` of a complex Hilbert space `E` and complex polynomials `p`, `q` with `q` free of zeros in the
closed unit disc, `q(T)` is invertible and `‖p(T) q(T)⁻¹‖ ≤ sup_{|ζ| = 1} |p(ζ)/q(ζ)|`. -/
theorem inequality_rational {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] {T : E →L[ℂ] E} (hT : ‖T‖ ≤ 1) (p q : ℂ[X])
    (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, ‖z‖ ≤ 1 → q.eval z ≠ 0) :
    IsUnit (aeval T q) ∧
      ‖aeval T p * Ring.inverse (aeval T q)‖ₑ ≤
        ⨆ ζ ∈ Metric.sphere (0 : ℂ) 1, ‖p.eval ζ / q.eval ζ‖ₑ := by
  sorry

/-- **Von Neumann's theorem for dissipative operators** ([HairerWanner1996], §IV.11). Let
`r = p/q` be a complex rational function without poles in the closed left half-plane. For every
bounded dissipative operator `A` of a complex Hilbert space and every `τ ≥ 0`, `q(τA)` is
invertible and `r(τA) = p(τA) q(τA)⁻¹` satisfies `‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ (sup_y |r(iy)|)ⁿ` for every `n`. -/
theorem inequality_dissipative {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] {A : E →L[ℂ] E} (hA : ∀ x, (⟪A x, x⟫_ℂ).re ≤ 0) (p q : ℂ[X])
    (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → q.eval z ≠ 0) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : 0 ≤ τ) :
    IsUnit (aeval ((τ : ℂ) • A) q) ∧ ∀ n : ℕ,
      ‖(aeval ((τ : ℂ) • A) p * Ring.inverse (aeval ((τ : ℂ) • A) q)) ^ n‖ₑ ≤
        (⨆ y : ℝ, ‖p.eval (y * Complex.I) / q.eval (y * Complex.I)‖ₑ) ^ n := by
  sorry

/-- **Von Neumann's theorem for m-dissipative operators**. Let `A` be a possibly unbounded
operator of a complex Hilbert space, dissipative (`re ⟪A x, x⟫ ≤ 0` on its domain) with `μ - A`
onto for some `μ > 0` (m-dissipative, [Pazy1983], §1.4), `r = p/q` a complex rational function
without poles in the closed left half-plane and bounded at infinity (`deg p ≤ deg q`), `N = deg q`
and `τ > 0`. Exactly one bounded
operator `S` satisfies `S (x - τAx) = x` on the domain, the resolvent `(1 - τA)⁻¹`;
`Q(S) = ∑_{k ≤ N} qₖ (S - 1)ᵏ S^{N-k}` is invertible, and `r(τA) = P(S) Q(S)⁻¹`,
`P(S) = ∑_{k ≤ N} pₖ (S - 1)ᵏ S^{N-k}`, satisfies `‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ (sup_y |r(iy)|)ⁿ` for every
`n`. -/
theorem inequality_mdissipative {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] {A : E →ₗ.[ℂ] E} (hA : ∀ x : A.domain, (⟪A x, (x : E)⟫_ℂ).re ≤ 0)
    (hA' : ∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ ∀ y : E, ∃ x : A.domain, (μ : ℂ) • (x : E) - A x = y)
    (p q : ℂ[X]) (hpq : p.natDegree ≤ q.natDegree) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → q.eval z ≠ 0)
    {τ : ℝ} (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    ∃ S : E →L[ℂ] E,
      (∀ T : E →L[ℂ] E, (∀ x : A.domain, T ((x : E) - (τ : ℂ) • A x) = x) ↔ T = S) ∧
      let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        p.coeff k • ((S - 1) ^ k * S ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        q.coeff k • ((S - 1) ^ k * S ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      IsUnit Q ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, ‖(P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n‖ₑ ≤
        (⨆ y : ℝ, ‖p.eval (y * Complex.I) / q.eval (y * Complex.I)‖ₑ) ^ n := by
  sorry

/-- **A-stable schemes are unconditionally stable** ([HairerWanner1996], §IV.11). Let
`r = p/q` be a real rational function without poles in the closed left half-plane. For every
bounded dissipative operator `A` of a Hilbert space over `𝕜 = ℝ` or `ℂ` and every `τ ≥ 0`,
`q(τA)` is invertible and `r(τA) = p(τA) q(τA)⁻¹` satisfies `‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ (sup_y |r(iy)|)ⁿ` for
every `n`. -/
theorem inequality_dissipative_real {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E] {A : E →L[𝕜] E}
    (hA : ∀ x, RCLike.re ⟪A x, x⟫_𝕜 ≤ 0) (p q : ℝ[X]) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0)
    {τ : ℝ} (hτ : 0 ≤ τ) :
    IsUnit (aeval ((τ : 𝕜) • A) (q.map (algebraMap ℝ 𝕜))) ∧ ∀ n : ℕ,
      ‖(aeval ((τ : 𝕜) • A) (p.map (algebraMap ℝ 𝕜)) *
          Ring.inverse (aeval ((τ : 𝕜) • A) (q.map (algebraMap ℝ 𝕜)))) ^ n‖ₑ ≤
        (⨆ y : ℝ, ‖aeval (y * Complex.I) p / aeval (y * Complex.I) q‖ₑ) ^ n := by
  sorry

/-- **A-stable schemes are unconditionally stable, for m-dissipative operators**: the real form
of `VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative`, over `𝕜 = ℝ` or `ℂ`. Let `A` be a
possibly unbounded operator of a Hilbert space over `𝕜`, dissipative
(`re ⟪A x, x⟫ ≤ 0` on its domain) with `μ - A` onto for some `μ > 0` (m-dissipative,
[Pazy1983], §1.4), `r = p/q` a real rational function without poles in the closed left
half-plane and bounded at infinity (`deg p ≤ deg q`), `N = deg q` and `τ > 0`. Exactly one
bounded operator `S` satisfies `S (x - τAx) = x` on the domain, the resolvent `(1 - τA)⁻¹`;
`Q(S) = ∑_{k ≤ N} qₖ (S - 1)ᵏ S^{N-k}` is invertible, and `r(τA) = P(S) Q(S)⁻¹`,
`P(S) = ∑_{k ≤ N} pₖ (S - 1)ᵏ S^{N-k}`, satisfies `‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ (sup_y |r(iy)|)ⁿ` for every `n`. -/
theorem inequality_mdissipative_real {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E] {A : E →ₗ.[𝕜] E}
    (hA : ∀ x : A.domain, RCLike.re ⟪A x, (x : E)⟫_𝕜 ≤ 0)
    (hA' : ∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ ∀ y : E, ∃ x : A.domain, (μ : 𝕜) • (x : E) - A x = y)
    (p q : ℝ[X]) (hpq : p.natDegree ≤ q.natDegree) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0)
    {τ : ℝ} (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    ∃ S : E →L[𝕜] E,
      (∀ T : E →L[𝕜] E, (∀ x : A.domain, T ((x : E) - (τ : 𝕜) • A x) = x) ↔ T = S) ∧
      let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        (p.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((S - 1) ^ k * S ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        (q.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((S - 1) ^ k * S ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      IsUnit Q ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, ‖(P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n‖ₑ ≤
        (⨆ y : ℝ, ‖aeval (y * Complex.I) p / aeval (y * Complex.I) q‖ₑ) ^ n := by
  sorry

/-- **The Cayley transform of an m-dissipative operator is a contraction**. Let `A` be a
possibly unbounded operator of a Hilbert space over `𝕜 = ℝ` or `ℂ`, dissipative
(`re ⟪A x, x⟫ ≤ 0` on its domain) with `μ - A` onto for some `μ > 0` (m-dissipative,
[Pazy1983], §1.4). For every `τ > 0`, exactly one bounded operator `T` satisfies
`T (x - τAx) = x + τAx` for all `x` in the domain, the Cayley transform
`C_τ = (1 + τA)(1 - τA)⁻¹`, and `‖C_τ‖ ≤ 1`. -/
theorem cayley_contraction {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E] {A : E →ₗ.[𝕜] E}
    (hA : ∀ x : A.domain, RCLike.re ⟪A x, (x : E)⟫_𝕜 ≤ 0)
    (hA' : ∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ ∀ y : E, ∃ x : A.domain, (μ : 𝕜) • (x : E) - A x = y) {τ : ℝ}
    (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    ∃ Cτ : E →L[𝕜] E, ‖Cτ‖ ≤ 1 ∧ ∀ T : E →L[𝕜] E,
      (∀ x : A.domain, T ((x : E) - (τ : 𝕜) • A x) = x + (τ : 𝕜) • A x) ↔ T = Cτ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of an A-stable scheme of order `m`** ([BrennerThomee1979]). Let `r = p/q` be a
complex rational function without poles in the closed left half-plane, A-stable
(`|r(iy)| ≤ 1`), of order `m` (`r(z) - e^z = O(z^{m+1})` at `0`). There is a constant `K` such
that, for every bounded dissipative operator `A` of a complex Hilbert space, every `τ ≥ 0`, `n`
and `x`, `‖r(τA)ⁿ x - e^{nτA} x‖ ≤ K nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖`. -/
theorem error_bound (p q : ℂ[X]) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → q.eval z ≠ 0)
    (hr : ∀ y : ℝ, ‖p.eval (y * Complex.I) / q.eval (y * Complex.I)‖ ≤ 1) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => p.eval z / q.eval z - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ K : ℝ, ∀ {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E] [CompleteSpace E]
      (A : E →L[ℂ] E), (∀ x, (⟪A x, x⟫_ℂ).re ≤ 0) → ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 ≤ τ → ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : E),
        ‖((aeval ((τ : ℂ) • A) p * Ring.inverse (aeval ((τ : ℂ) • A) q)) ^ n) x -
            NormedSpace.exp (((n * τ : ℝ) : ℂ) • A) x‖ ≤
          K * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖(A ^ (m + 1)) x‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of an A-stable scheme of order `m`, real coefficients** ([BrennerThomee1979]).
Let `r = p/q` be a real rational function without poles in the closed left half-plane, A-stable
(`|r(iy)| ≤ 1`), of order `m` (`r(z) - e^z = O(z^{m+1})` at `0`). There is a constant `K` such
that, for every bounded dissipative operator `A` of a Hilbert space over `𝕜 = ℝ` or `ℂ`, every
`τ ≥ 0`, `n` and `x`, `‖r(τA)ⁿ x - e^{nτA} x‖ ≤ K nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖`. -/
theorem error_bound_real (p q : ℝ[X]) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0)
    (hr : ∀ y : ℝ, ‖aeval (y * Complex.I) p / aeval (y * Complex.I) q‖ ≤ 1) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => aeval z p / aeval z q - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ K : ℝ, ∀ {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E]
      [CompleteSpace E] (A : E →L[𝕜] E), (∀ x, RCLike.re ⟪A x, x⟫_𝕜 ≤ 0) →
      ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 ≤ τ → ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : E),
        ‖((aeval ((τ : 𝕜) • A) (p.map (algebraMap ℝ 𝕜)) *
              Ring.inverse (aeval ((τ : 𝕜) • A) (q.map (algebraMap ℝ 𝕜)))) ^ n) x -
            NormedSpace.exp (((n * τ : ℝ) : 𝕜) • A) x‖ ≤
          K * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖(A ^ (m + 1)) x‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of an A-stable scheme of order `m` for m-dissipative operators**
([BrennerThomee1979]). Let `r = p/q` be a complex rational function without poles
in the closed left half-plane, A-stable (`|r(iy)| ≤ 1`), of order `m`
(`r(z) - e^z = O(z^{m+1})` at `0`). There is a constant `K` such that for every possibly
unbounded operator `A` of a complex Hilbert space, dissipative with `μ - A` onto for some
`μ > 0` (m-dissipative, [Pazy1983], §1.4): there is a family `S` of bounded operators, `S 0 = 1`,
whose orbits `t ↦ S t x` from `x ∈ D(A)` are strong solutions of `u' = A u`, and the only ones
(the semigroup `e^{tA}`), such that for every `τ > 0`, with the resolvent `R = (1 - τA)⁻¹` (the
only bounded operator mapping `x - τAx` to `x`) and `r(τA) = P(R) Q(R)⁻¹` as in
`VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative`, `‖r(τA)ⁿ x - e^{nτA} x‖ ≤ K nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖` for every
`n` and `x ∈ D(A^{m+1})` (a chain `u 0 = x, …, u (m + 1) = A^{m+1} x` in the graph of `A`). -/
theorem error_bound_mdissipative (p q : ℂ[X]) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → q.eval z ≠ 0)
    (hr : ∀ y : ℝ, ‖p.eval (y * Complex.I) / q.eval (y * Complex.I)‖ ≤ 1) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => p.eval z / q.eval z - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ K : ℝ, ∀ {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E] [CompleteSpace E]
      (A : E →ₗ.[ℂ] E), (∀ x : A.domain, (⟪A x, (x : E)⟫_ℂ).re ≤ 0) →
      (∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ ∀ y : E, ∃ x : A.domain, (μ : ℂ) • (x : E) - A x = y) →
      ∃ S : ℝ → E →L[ℂ] E, S 0 = 1 ∧
        (∀ (x : A.domain) (T : ℝ), IsStrongSolution A (Set.Icc 0 T) fun t => S t x) ∧
        (∀ (x : A.domain) (T : ℝ) (u : ℝ → E), u 0 = x → IsStrongSolution A (Set.Icc 0 T) u →
          Set.EqOn u (fun t => S t x) (Set.Icc 0 T)) ∧
        ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ → ∃ R : E →L[ℂ] E,
          (∀ T : E →L[ℂ] E, (∀ x : A.domain, T ((x : E) - (τ : ℂ) • A x) = x) ↔ T = R) ∧
          let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
            p.coeff k • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
          let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
            q.coeff k • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
          ∀ (n : ℕ) (u : ℕ → E), (∀ j < m + 1, (u j, u (j + 1)) ∈ A.graph) →
            ‖((P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n) (u 0) - S (n * τ) (u 0)‖ ≤
              K * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖u (m + 1)‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of an A-stable scheme of order `m` for m-dissipative operators, real
coefficients** ([BrennerThomee1979]): the real form of
`VonNeumann.error_bound_mdissipative`, over `𝕜 = ℝ` or `ℂ`. Let `r = p/q` be a real rational
function without poles in the closed left half-plane, A-stable (`|r(iy)| ≤ 1`), of order `m`
(`r(z) - e^z = O(z^{m+1})` at `0`). There is a constant `K` such that for every m-dissipative,
possibly unbounded, operator `A` of a Hilbert space over `𝕜`, with its semigroup `S` (as in
`VonNeumann.error_bound_mdissipative`), every `τ > 0` and `r(τA) = P(R) Q(R)⁻¹` at the resolvent
`R = (1 - τA)⁻¹`, `‖r(τA)ⁿ x - e^{nτA} x‖ ≤ K nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖` for every `n` and
`x ∈ D(A^{m+1})`. -/
theorem error_bound_mdissipative_real (p q : ℝ[X]) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0)
    (hr : ∀ y : ℝ, ‖aeval (y * Complex.I) p / aeval (y * Complex.I) q‖ ≤ 1) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => aeval z p / aeval z q - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ K : ℝ, ∀ {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E]
      [CompleteSpace E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 E] (A : E →ₗ.[𝕜] E),
      (∀ x : A.domain, RCLike.re ⟪A x, (x : E)⟫_𝕜 ≤ 0) →
      (∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ ∀ y : E, ∃ x : A.domain, (μ : 𝕜) • (x : E) - A x = y) →
      ∃ S : ℝ → E →L[𝕜] E, S 0 = 1 ∧
        (∀ (x : A.domain) (T : ℝ), IsStrongSolution A (Set.Icc 0 T) fun t => S t x) ∧
        (∀ (x : A.domain) (T : ℝ) (u : ℝ → E), u 0 = x → IsStrongSolution A (Set.Icc 0 T) u →
          Set.EqOn u (fun t => S t x) (Set.Icc 0 T)) ∧
        ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ → ∃ R : E →L[𝕜] E,
          (∀ T : E →L[𝕜] E, (∀ x : A.domain, T ((x : E) - (τ : 𝕜) • A x) = x) ↔ T = R) ∧
          let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
            (p.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
          let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
            (q.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
          ∀ (n : ℕ) (u : ℕ → E), (∀ j < m + 1, (u j, u (j + 1)) ∈ A.graph) →
            ‖((P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n) (u 0) - S (n * τ) (u 0)‖ ≤
              K * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖u (m + 1)‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of an A-stable scheme of order `m` for quasi-contractive semigroups**
([BrennerThomee1979]; [Pazy1983], §1.5, §3.1). Let `r = p/q` be a real rational function
without poles in the closed left half-plane, A-stable (`|r(iy)| ≤ 1`), of order `m`
(`r(z) - e^z = O(z^{m+1})` at `0`). There are `c₀ > 0`, `K` and `κ`, depending on `r` only, such
that for every possibly unbounded operator `A` of a Hilbert space over `𝕜` with
`re ⟪A x, x⟫ ≤ ω ‖x‖²` (`ω ≥ 0`) and `μ - A` onto for some `μ > ω` (`A - ω` m-dissipative; for
instance `L + B` for an m-dissipative `L` and a bounded `B`, `ω = ‖B‖`): there is a family `S`
of bounded operators, `S 0 = 1`, `‖S t‖ ≤ e^{ωt}`, whose orbits from `D(A)` are strong solutions
of `u' = A u`, and the only ones (the semigroup `e^{tA}`), such that for every `τ > 0` with
`ωτ ≤ c₀`, with the resolvent `R = (1 - τA)⁻¹` and `r(τA) = P(R) Q(R)⁻¹` as in
`VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative`, `‖r(τA)ⁿ x - e^{nτA} x‖ ≤ K e^{κωnτ} nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖` for
every `n` and `x ∈ D(A^{m+1})`. -/
theorem error_bound_quasi_real (p q : ℝ[X]) (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0)
    (hr : ∀ y : ℝ, ‖aeval (y * Complex.I) p / aeval (y * Complex.I) q‖ ≤ 1) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => aeval z p / aeval z q - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ c₀ K κ : ℝ, 0 < c₀ ∧ ∀ {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E]
      [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 E]
      (A : E →ₗ.[𝕜] E) (ω : ℝ), 0 ≤ ω →
      (∀ x : A.domain, RCLike.re ⟪A x, (x : E)⟫_𝕜 ≤ ω * ‖(x : E)‖ ^ 2) →
      (∃ μ : ℝ, ω < μ ∧ ∀ y : E, ∃ x : A.domain, (μ : 𝕜) • (x : E) - A x = y) →
      ∃ S : ℝ → E →L[𝕜] E, S 0 = 1 ∧ (∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ‖S t‖ ≤ Real.exp (ω * t)) ∧
        (∀ (x : A.domain) (T : ℝ), IsStrongSolution A (Set.Icc 0 T) fun t => S t x) ∧
        (∀ (x : A.domain) (T : ℝ) (u : ℝ → E), u 0 = x → IsStrongSolution A (Set.Icc 0 T) u →
          Set.EqOn u (fun t => S t x) (Set.Icc 0 T)) ∧
        ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ → ω * τ ≤ c₀ → ∃ R : E →L[𝕜] E,
          (∀ T : E →L[𝕜] E, (∀ x : A.domain, T ((x : E) - (τ : 𝕜) • A x) = x) ↔ T = R) ∧
          let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
            (p.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
          let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
            (q.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
          ∀ (n : ℕ) (u : ℕ → E), (∀ j < m + 1, (u j, u (j + 1)) ∈ A.graph) →
            ‖((P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n) (u 0) - S (n * τ) (u 0)‖ ≤
              K * Real.exp (κ * ω * (n * τ)) * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖u (m + 1)‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The Hille–Yosida estimates** ([Pazy1983], §1.5). Let `S` be a strongly continuous
semigroup of bounded operators of a complex Banach space (`S 0 = 1`, `S (s + t) = S s S t` and
`t ↦ S t x` continuous for `s, t ≥ 0`) with `‖S t‖ ≤ M e^{ωt}` for `t ≥ 0`, and generator `A`:
`x ∈ D(A)` with `A x = y` iff `t ↦ S t x` has right derivative `y` at `0`. Every `z` with
`re z > ω` is in the resolvent set of `A`: there is a bounded `R` with `R (z x - A x) = x` on
`D(A)` and `R y ∈ D(A)`, `A R y = z R y - y`, and `‖Rᵐ‖ ≤ M/(re z - ω)ᵐ` for every `m`. -/
theorem resolvent_estimates_banach {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℂ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] (S : ℝ → E →L[ℂ] E) (hS0 : S 0 = 1)
    (hSadd : ∀ s t : ℝ, 0 ≤ s → 0 ≤ t → S (s + t) = S s * S t)
    (hSc : ∀ x : E, ContinuousOn (fun t => S t x) (Set.Ici 0)) {M ω : ℝ}
    (hSb : ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ‖S t‖ ≤ M * Real.exp (ω * t)) (z : ℂ) (hz : ω < z.re) :
    ∃ R : E →L[ℂ] E,
      (∀ x y : E, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t x) y (Set.Ici 0) 0 → R (z • x - y) = x) ∧
      (∀ y : E, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t (R y)) (z • R y - y) (Set.Ici 0) 0) ∧
      ∀ m : ℕ, ‖R ^ m‖ ≤ M / (z.re - ω) ^ m := by
  sorry

/-- **Backward Euler on Banach spaces** ([BrennerThomee1979]; [Pazy1983], §1.5). Let `S` be a
strongly continuous semigroup of a Banach space over `𝕜` with `‖S t‖ ≤ M e^{ωt}` (`ω ≥ 0`) and
generator `A` (as in `VonNeumann.resolvent_estimates_banach`), `τ > 0` with `ωτ < 1`, and `R`
with `R (x - τ A x) = x` on `D(A)`. Backward Euler, `r(z) = 1/(1 - z)`, is `r(τA) = R`. It is
stable, `‖Rᵏ‖ ≤ M/(1 - ωτ)ᵏ` (the Hille–Yosida estimates), and for every `n` and
`x ∈ D(A²)` (a chain `u 0 = x, u 1 = A x, u 2 = A² x` of right derivatives)
`‖Rⁿ x - S(nτ) x‖ ≤ (M/(1 - ωτ)ⁿ) (M/(1 - ωτ) + M e^{ωnτ}/2) M e^{ωnτ} nτ τ ‖A² x‖`. -/
theorem error_bound_backward_euler_banach {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [NormedSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 E]
    (S : ℝ → E →L[𝕜] E) (hS0 : S 0 = 1)
    (hSadd : ∀ s t : ℝ, 0 ≤ s → 0 ≤ t → S (s + t) = S s * S t)
    (hSc : ∀ x : E, ContinuousOn (fun t => S t x) (Set.Ici 0)) {M ω : ℝ} (hω : 0 ≤ ω)
    (hSb : ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ‖S t‖ ≤ M * Real.exp (ω * t)) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : 0 < τ)
    (hωτ : ω * τ < 1) (R : E →L[𝕜] E)
    (hR : ∀ x y : E, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t x) y (Set.Ici 0) 0 → R (x - (τ : 𝕜) • y) = x) :
    (∀ k : ℕ, ‖R ^ k‖ ≤ M / (1 - ω * τ) ^ k) ∧
      ∀ (n : ℕ) (u : ℕ → E),
        (∀ j < 2, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t (u j)) (u (j + 1)) (Set.Ici 0) 0) →
        ‖(R ^ n) (u 0) - S (n * τ) (u 0)‖ ≤ M / (1 - ω * τ) ^ n *
          (M / (1 - ω * τ) + M * Real.exp (ω * (n * τ)) / 2) * (M * Real.exp (ω * (n * τ))) *
            (n * τ) * τ * ‖u 2‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of a stable scheme of order `m` on Banach spaces, from the Hille–Yosida
estimates** ([BrennerThomee1979]; [Thomee2006], Ch. 9). Let `r = p/q` be as in
`VonNeumann.error_bound_banach_real`, of order `m`, with remainder `ρ`. There are `c > 0`,
depending on `r` and `m` only, and for every `M` a `K₀`, depending on `r`, `m` and `M` only, such
that for every strongly continuous semigroup `S` of a Banach space over `𝕜` with
`‖S t‖ ≤ M e^{ωt}` (`ω ≥ 0`) and generator `A` (as in `VonNeumann.resolvent_estimates_banach`),
every `τ > 0` with `ωτ ≤ c` and `R` with `R (x - τ A x) = x` on `D(A)` (the resolvent
`(1 - τA)⁻¹`), with `r(τA) = P(R) Q(R)⁻¹` and `ρ(τA) = P_ρ(R) Q(R)⁻¹`: `Q(R)` is invertible,
`‖ρ(τA)‖ ≤ K₀`, and if `‖r(τA)ᵏ‖ ≤ Mₛ` for `k ≤ n`, then
`‖r(τA)ⁿ x - S(nτ) x‖ ≤ Mₛ (K₀ + M e^{ωnτ}/(m+1)!) M e^{ωnτ} nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖` for every
`x ∈ D(A^{m+1})`. Compared with `VonNeumann.error_bound_banach_real`, the invertibility of
`Q(R)`, the injectivity of `R` and the remainder bound are conclusions, for the price of a growth
bound on all of `t ≥ 0` and of `ωτ ≤ c`. -/
theorem error_bound_banach_real_hille_yosida (p q : ℝ[X]) (hpq : p.natDegree ≤ q.natDegree)
    (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => aeval z p / aeval z q - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 < c ∧ ∀ M : ℝ, ∃ K₀ : ℝ, ∀ {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E]
      [NormedSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 E]
      (S : ℝ → E →L[𝕜] E), S 0 = 1 → (∀ s t : ℝ, 0 ≤ s → 0 ≤ t → S (s + t) = S s * S t) →
      (∀ x : E, ContinuousOn (fun t => S t x) (Set.Ici 0)) → ∀ ω : ℝ, 0 ≤ ω →
      (∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ‖S t‖ ≤ M * Real.exp (ω * t)) → ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ → ω * τ ≤ c →
      ∀ R : E →L[𝕜] E,
      (∀ x y : E, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t x) y (Set.Ici 0) 0 → R (x - (τ : 𝕜) • y) = x) →
      let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        (p.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        (q.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      let ρ : ℝ[X] := (p - q * ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (m + 1), C (1 / (j.factorial : ℝ)) * X ^ j) /ₘ
        X ^ (m + 1)
      let Pρ := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
        (ρ.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
      IsUnit Q ∧ ‖Pρ * Ring.inverse Q‖ ≤ K₀ ∧
        ∀ (n : ℕ) (Ms : ℝ), (∀ k ≤ n, ‖(P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ k‖ ≤ Ms) →
        ∀ u : ℕ → E,
          (∀ j < m + 1, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t (u j)) (u (j + 1)) (Set.Ici 0) 0) →
          ‖((P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n) (u 0) - S (n * τ) (u 0)‖ ≤
            Ms * (K₀ + M * Real.exp (ω * (n * τ)) / (m + 1).factorial) *
              (M * Real.exp (ω * (n * τ))) * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖u (m + 1)‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **The error of a stable scheme of order `m` on Banach spaces** ([BrennerThomee1979];
[Thomee2006], Ch. 9). Let `S` be a strongly continuous semigroup of bounded operators of a
Banach space over `𝕜` (`S 0 = 1`, `S (s + t) = S s S t` and `t ↦ S t x` continuous for
`s, t ≥ 0`), with generator `A`: `x ∈ D(A)` with `A x = y` iff `t ↦ S t x` has right derivative
`y` at `0`. Let `r = p/q` be a real rational function with `deg p ≤ deg q`, without poles in the
closed left half-plane, of order `m`, with remainder `ρ = (p - q Tₘ)/X^{m+1}`,
`Tₘ = Σ_{j≤m} Xʲ/j!`. Let `τ ≥ 0` and `R` injective with `R (x - τ A x) = x` on `D(A)` (the
resolvent `(1 - τA)⁻¹`), and `r(τA) = P(R) Q(R)⁻¹`, `ρ(τA) = P_ρ(R) Q(R)⁻¹` as in
`VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative`, `Q(R)` invertible. Off Hilbert spaces stability is not
automatic (von Neumann's inequality fails); if `‖r(τA)ᵏ‖ ≤ Mₛ` for `k ≤ n`, `‖ρ(τA)‖ ≤ K₀` and
`‖S t‖ ≤ M` on `[0, nτ]`, then `‖r(τA)ⁿ x - S(nτ) x‖ ≤ Mₛ (K₀ + M/(m+1)!) M nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖`
for every `x ∈ D(A^{m+1})` (a chain `u 0 = x, …, u (m + 1) = A^{m+1} x` of right derivatives). -/
theorem error_bound_banach_real (p q : ℝ[X]) (hpq : p.natDegree ≤ q.natDegree)
    (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => aeval z p / aeval z q - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1))
    {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace 𝕜 E] [CompleteSpace E]
    [NormedSpace ℝ E] [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 E] (S : ℝ → E →L[𝕜] E) (hS0 : S 0 = 1)
    (hSadd : ∀ s t : ℝ, 0 ≤ s → 0 ≤ t → S (s + t) = S s * S t)
    (hSc : ∀ x : E, ContinuousOn (fun t => S t x) (Set.Ici 0)) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : 0 ≤ τ)
    (R : E →L[𝕜] E)
    (hR : ∀ x y : E, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t x) y (Set.Ici 0) 0 → R (x - (τ : 𝕜) • y) = x)
    (hRi : Function.Injective R) :
    let P := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
      (p.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
    let Q := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
      (q.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
    let ρ : ℝ[X] := (p - q * ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (m + 1), C (1 / (j.factorial : ℝ)) * X ^ j) /ₘ
      X ^ (m + 1)
    let Pρ := ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (q.natDegree + 1),
      (ρ.coeff k : 𝕜) • ((R - 1) ^ k * R ^ (q.natDegree - k))
    IsUnit Q → ∀ (n : ℕ) (Ms M K₀ : ℝ), (∀ k ≤ n, ‖(P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ k‖ ≤ Ms) →
      (∀ t ∈ Set.Icc 0 (n * τ), ‖S t‖ ≤ M) → ‖Pρ * Ring.inverse Q‖ ≤ K₀ →
      ∀ u : ℕ → E, (∀ j < m + 1, HasDerivWithinAt (fun t => S t (u j)) (u (j + 1)) (Set.Ici 0) 0) →
        ‖((P * Ring.inverse Q) ^ n) (u 0) - S (n * τ) (u 0)‖ ≤
          Ms * (K₀ + M / (m + 1).factorial) * M * (n * τ) * τ ^ m * ‖u (m + 1)‖ := by
  sorry

/-- **Brenner–Thomée's `√n` stability bound, and the `√n`-lossy error bound, for bounded
semigroups on Banach spaces** ([BrennerThomee1979] for the stability bound). Let `r = p/q` be a
real rational function with `deg p ≤ deg q`, without poles in the closed left half-plane,
A-stable (`|r(iy)| ≤ 1`), with `|r(∞)| < 1` (`|p_N| < |q_N|`, `N = deg q`), of order `m`. There
are constants `C ≥ 0` and `K`, depending on `r` only, such that for every strongly continuous
semigroup `S` of a Banach space over `𝕜 = ℝ` or `ℂ`, bounded (`‖S t‖ ≤ M` for `t ≥ 0`), with
generator `A` (right derivatives at `0`), and every `τ > 0`: exactly one bounded operator `R` satisfies
`R (x - τAx) = x` on `D(A)` (the resolvent `(1 - τA)⁻¹`); `Q(R)` is invertible; `r(τA) = P(R) Q(R)⁻¹` (as in
`VonNeumann.inequality_mdissipative`) satisfies `‖r(τA)ⁿ‖ ≤ M (1 + C √n)` for every `n`; and
`‖r(τA)ⁿ x - S(nτ) x‖ ≤ K M³ (1 + C √n) nτ τᵐ ‖A^{m+1} x‖` for every `n` and `x ∈ D(A^{m+1})` (a
chain `u 0 = x, …, u (m + 1) = A^{m+1} x` of right derivatives). The error bound is the
stability bound times consistency: at fixed `T = nτ` it is of order `m - 1/2`, weaker by `√n`
than the smooth-data estimates of the sources (`O(τᵐ)` for `x ∈ D(A^{m+2})` [HershKato1979]),
which are not formalized; the case `|r(∞)| = 1` is not covered. -/
theorem error_bound_banach_sqrt (p q : ℝ[X]) (hpq : p.natDegree ≤ q.natDegree)
    (hq : ∀ z : ℂ, z.re ≤ 0 → aeval z q ≠ 0)
    (hr : ∀ y : ℝ, ‖aeval (y * Complex.I) p / aeval (y * Complex.I) q‖ ≤ 1)
    (hinf : |p.coeff q.natDegree| < |q.leadingCoeff|) {m : ℕ}
    (hm : (fun z : ℂ => aeval z p / aeval z q - Complex.exp z) =O[𝓝 0] fun z => z ^ (m + 1)) :
    ∃ C K : ℝ, 0 ≤ C ∧ ∀ {𝕜 E : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace 𝕜 E]
      [CompleteSpace E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 E]
      (S : ℝ → E →L[𝕜] E) (M : ℝ), S 0 = 1 →
      (∀ s t : ℝ, 0 ≤ s → 0 ≤ t → S (s + t) = S s * S t) →
